        <mxCell id="61Upp6UU6CLk61KUn04W-3" parent="RBY09DncccYwnFpq-k9D-1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;rounded=0;fontColor=light-dark(#000000,#000000);fontSize=15;" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 17px;&quot;&gt;Notes&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;:&amp;nbsp;&lt;div&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Desired date range: 10/1/2022 to 6/30/2026.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;CIH acupuncture user is defined using SQL code provided by Steven Zeliadt and Jamie Douglas at the VA.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;The final step of their code produces a distinct patient-visit table. This table will be used to identify the acupuncture users from the larger datasets requested in the diagrams shown here.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;If the data requested may be too large to extract/store for all VA users, the requested tables could 1st be filtered to just those using acupuncture based on the &#39;VA CIH Users&#39; datasets.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Age is calculated when the data is pulled so something I need to remember for services that take place years before.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="249" width="638" x="27" y="85" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
